; A declared type named as a Rust container cannot capture the generated
; code, which writes every container fully qualified. An intrinsic's own
; name, such as Result, is refused as a declaration. A declared Box is not
; shown here: datom-codec's derive writes Box::new unqualified in every
; enum's datomization, so a Box in the module captures it.
